       These functions copy the (null-terminated) _c_h_s_t_r array into the  window
       image structure starting at the current cursor position.

       The four functions with _n as the last argument copy at most _n elements,
       but no more than will fit on the line.  If nn=--11 then the whole array is
       copied, to the maximum number of characters that will fit on the line.

       The  window  cursor  is  _n_o_t advanced.  These functions are faster than
       wwaaddddnnssttrr.  On the other hand:

       •   they do not perform checking (such as for the  newline,  backspace,
           or carriage return characters),

       •   they do not advance the current cursor position,

       •   they do not expand other control characters to ^-escapes, and

       •   they  truncate  the  string  if it crosses the right margin, rather
           than wrapping it around to the new line.

